{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe underestimation of upward momentum: When sentiment history shows consecutive high values (1.00) or a rising trend, the model's flat/linear forecast fails to capture immediate price spikes (e.g., 70->76). Apply a positive bias adjustment of +4 to +6 EUR for the first 5-7 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "Implement aggressive mean reversion after peaks: The model consistently lags in predicting the decline following a price spike (overshoot). When the forecast predicts a slow decline while true prices are volatile, apply a steeper negative slope correction starting from day 4 to day 10 to account for the rapid drop from ~76 to ~70.",
    "Adjust for sentiment lag in volatility: High sentiment scores (1.00) in the history often precede a 3-5 day delay in price reaction. Do not rely on the model's immediate reaction to sentiment; instead, delay the upward price adjustment by 2 days and then accelerate it.",
    "Horizon-specific decay correction: The model assumes a near-constant price or very slow drift. For horizons beyond 10 days, the model fails to capture the eventual downward trend seen in the true outcomes (dropping to ~67). Apply a linear downward correction of -0.5 to -0.8 EUR per day for days 15-30 to align with the observed mean reversion to the 67-68 range."
  ]
}
